=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, ribonn TE, neurons ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.0037
  lasso keeps 47 of 61 codons; sets 14 to exactly 0: TCC, TGC, CTA, CCT, CCC, CCA, CCG, CGT, CGG, ACG, GTT, GCC, GAG, GGG
  of those 14, 14 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 61 nominally significant codons overall, 47 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9923, Spearman rho = 0.9842; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.932 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS -52.327 / 3.679, lasso -0.330 / 3.441
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS 52.0616, lasso 0.0795

